/* The way into the advanced search from the header's quick search: a bar
   hung under the box, shown while the field has focus and nothing worth
   searching for has been typed.
 *
 * It is its own element rather than the button above, which the theme
 * turns into the magnifier inside the box for every widget on the site
 * (.wis-search-widget .wis-mini-advanced-button in _search.css, with
 * `!block` that also defeats .is-hidden). The design draws the magnifier
 * AND this bar, so the two cannot be one element.
 *
 * Drawn only in the header and only from xl up: the in-page boxes have no
 * quick search to offer it from, and below 1280px the magnifier itself
 * becomes this bar - see the is-quick-open rules in the small-screen
 * sheet - which would otherwise draw two of them. */

@media (width >= 1280px) {

  /* The arrow points away from the field's start edge, whichever edge that
     is - the same turn the small-screen bar makes. */

  /* Focus is drawn around the whole box rather than the field inside it.
     The field, the magnifier beside it and the bar under it are one
     control here, and a ring around the field alone ran between the field
     and the bar - two edges a pixel apart, which is what it looked like.
     No offset, so the ring sits on the box's own outline instead of
     floating outside it. */
  /* The field's focus ring, in the two numbers the bar under it also has
     to know: it begins where the ring's outer edge is, or the two draw
     edges a pixel or two apart and the pair looks askew. Same ring the
     base rule draws on every field; written again here only so the bar
     can be measured from it. */
  header[role="banner"] .wis-search-box-wrap {
    --wis-mini-focus-ring: 2px;
    /* No offset here, unlike the base rule: a ring standing a pixel off
       the field leaves a hairline between the field's own edge and the
       ring - most visible on the end side, where the divider to the
       magnifier sits right beside it. Flush against the field instead. */
    --wis-mini-focus-offset: 0px;
  }

  header[role="banner"] .wis-mini-search-input:focus {
    outline: var(--wis-mini-focus-ring) solid var(--color-maincolor, #161616);
    outline-offset: var(--wis-mini-focus-offset);
  }
}

